roofline control variant `fused_c1` / `fused_c1_layer` of workloads/clusterfusion_llama2_7b_decoder.yaml (applied by the
runner in the worktree roofline/build/src/ClusterFusion__clusterfusion__cluster_size_1/, never in third_party/).
Combined diff against the pin = patches/clusterfusion__residual_out.patch + the three changes below.
1. config.h: CLUSTER_SIZE 4 -> 1 (one CTA per head, no DSMEM; the cluster reduce loops run zero rounds).
2. kernel_sglang.cuh: correctness fix of the RMSNorm prologue for DIM_PER_BLOCK = HIDDEN_DIM / CLUSTER_SIZE >
   BLOCK_SIZE * 8 = 1024. Upstream keeps x + residual only in registers of the last loop iteration, so with
   CLUSTER_SIZE 1 (4 iterations) the normalisation loop would write the last chunk for every chunk. The fix stages
   x + residual in input_shmem (same thread, same addresses; no barrier needed) and reloads it before normalising.
   For CLUSTER_SIZE 4 (one iteration) it would be a no-op on the results; fused_c4 is built without it.
3. (= residual_out patch) input + residual is written to a new `residual_output` tensor instead of back into
   `residual`: the in-place write raced across the 32 head clusters (confirmed on GPU in R4; precedent: upstream's
   kernel_batch_sglang.cuh). See that patch's header.
4. (= fix 2 of patches/clusterfusion__residual_out_c4_fix.patch, same four lines) block.sync() at the top of the Q, K, V
   GEMV loops and the flash-decoding loop of kernel_sglang.cuh: upstream refills TMA buffer id % 2 while warps 1-3 may
   still read tile id - 2 from it. Confirmed as the remaining race of the cluster-4 build on GPU 3 (wrong k/v rows of
   warps 1-3 in heads 6, 7, 30, 31; 0/600 deviating launches after the fix); not observed in this cluster-1 build
   (0/600 deviating launches without it, 200 per S = 1k/4k/16k), added so that both fused builds run the same code
   apart from CLUSTER_SIZE and the prologue fix.
